# Git delegation

Applies to **this hub git repo** (the folder that contains `Agents/AGENTS.md` and `.cursor/hooks/`).

- In **this hub repo**, do **not** run `git` or `gh` in the parent agent shell. Delegate to **git-coordinator**; relay user choices; trust the **Git Report**.
- **Resume** the same git-coordinator agent id for `Yes` / `No` / `Preview`, `git add all`, `[custom]` / `[agent]`, and merge ids. Do not spawn a new Task per relay unless the last run aborted.
- Git commands start with **`git`** (`git add`, `git commit`, `git push`, `git auto push`). If the user says `add`, `commit`, `push`, or another git verb without `git`, ask if they want Git Coordinator and suggest `git <keyword>` next time. Do not run it until they say yes.
- **`git auto push`:** ask `about to add, commit and push all modified files to current repo. Are you sure?` Options: **Yes**, **No**, **Preview**.
- **`git commit`** with nothing staged starts **`git add`** in every repo, including sibling apps. List each file and a one-line summary. Wait for **`git add all`** or named paths. A sentence that describes the work is not that approval.
- **`git push`** with nothing staged, and files modified, starts **`git add`** and asks whether to commit first. **`git add all`** or named paths commit those files, then push. **No** pushes the current branch and does not commit. Files already staged are committed, then pushed.
- In **any other git repo** (sibling app, unrelated clone), the parent **may** run `git`/`gh`. The shell hook does not block those roots. The add list still applies before a commit. Do not stage files until they reply **`git add all`** or name the paths. Optional: use git-coordinator with `repo_path`.
- Ask which **repo_path** when the user wants coordinator on a specific repo. Orchestration: `Agents/Subagents/subagents.md`.
